# Harness specification

## Purpose

Enable an external AI agent to implement direct requests or feature
specifications within the project's agreed boundaries. The agent must report
the outcome of checks and tests rather than claiming unverified compliance.

## Requirements

- Follow the domain-oriented modular monolith in
  [architecture](../architecture.md) and the project
  [conventions](../conventions.md).
- Record every top-level domain package in `harness.yaml`.
- Implement requested behavior and cover acceptance criteria and important
  failures with focused tests. Ask about consequential missing requirements.
- Run `fastapi-harness check` and relevant tests. Resolve failures caused by
  the change and report pre-existing failures or checks that cannot run.
- Do not leak sensitive information in responses, logs, traces or external
  tools. Add observability only as required by the project.

## Verification

`fastapi-harness check` validates package registration, cyclomatic complexity,
strict MyPy typing, Ruff E and F lint rules,
and Ruff formatting for the application package. It does not execute tests,
validate every FastAPI practice or verify OpenTelemetry. Review those aspects
and run relevant tests separately.
